IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `spr-seat`

-- State Pension Regulations 2015 (S.I. 2015/173) -- WORKED CASES FOR THE SEAT LAYER (spr-seat.l4).
-- Each case is a person in the seat asking one of the seat's questions with plain answers. Every expected value is written by hand from the text
-- (the line of the source is in the comment), never copied from the encoding's output. At least one case for every question; the cases that sit
-- outside the encoding assert an explicit "not covered" value (fork F10, F21, F27 in NOTES.md).
-- Arguments are given in the order of the question's inputs.


§ `Part 1 and 1A -- whether the Regulations apply, who is a spouse, the full rate`

-- Line 15: reg 1(3). A person who reaches pensionable age on 5 April 2016, the day before the Regulations come into force, is outside them.
#ASSERT `Do these Regulations apply to me` (Date 5 4 2016) EQUALS `these Regulations do not apply to the person, who reached pensionable age before 6 April 2016`
-- Reaching pensionable age on 6 April 2016 itself is not before it.
#ASSERT `Do these Regulations apply to me` (Date 6 4 2016) EQUALS `these Regulations apply to the person`
#ASSERT `Do these Regulations apply to me` (Date 1 1 2031) EQUALS `these Regulations apply to the person`
-- Lines 13-22: reg 1(5). Married, and neither married to anyone else: counted as married.
#ASSERT `Does the law count the other person and me as spouses or civil partners` `married to each other` FALSE
-- Married to each other but one of them is also married to a third person: treated as not married to each other.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the law count the other person and me as spouses or civil partners` `married to each other` TRUE)
-- Fork F2: only a marriage is taken away; civil partners stay civil partners.
#ASSERT `Does the law count the other person and me as spouses or civil partners` `civil partners of each other` TRUE
-- Neither married nor civil partners.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the law count the other person and me as spouses or civil partners` `not married to each other and not civil partners` FALSE)
-- Line 25: reg 1A, 241.30 pounds a week.
#ASSERT `What is the full weekly rate of the State Pension` EQUALS 241.30

§ `Part 2 -- prisoners`

-- Lines 28-31: regs 2(1), 2(2)(a). In legal custody in Great Britain as a result of criminal proceedings, not remanded: withheld.
#ASSERT `Can my State Pension be withheld for a day I am in custody` (Date 1 6 2027) `imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings` TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE FALSE `a sentence of none of those kinds` FALSE FALSE
-- Reg 2(2)(b): unlawfully at large.
#ASSERT `Can my State Pension be withheld for a day I am in custody` (Date 1 6 2027) `unlawfully at large` TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE FALSE `a sentence of none of those kinds` FALSE FALSE
-- Reg 2(2)(d): detained under section 136 of the 2003 Act, in Great Britain.
#ASSERT `Can my State Pension be withheld for a day I am in custody` (Date 1 6 2027) `detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003` TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE FALSE `a sentence of none of those kinds` FALSE FALSE
-- Reg 2(2)(c): under section 47, on or before the certified release date (the day is before it).
#ASSERT `Can my State Pension be withheld for a day I am in custody` (Date 1 6 2027) `detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983` TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 2 6 2027) FALSE FALSE `a sentence of none of those kinds` FALSE FALSE
-- A day after the certified release date: not a prisoner by 2(2)(c)(ii).
#ASSERT NOT (`Can my State Pension be withheld for a day I am in custody` (Date 3 6 2027) `detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983` TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 2 6 2027) FALSE FALSE `a sentence of none of those kinds` FALSE FALSE)
-- Not in any of those kinds of custody.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can my State Pension be withheld for a day I am in custody` (Date 1 6 2027) `in none of those kinds of custody` TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE FALSE `a sentence of none of those kinds` FALSE FALSE)
-- Line 38: reg 2(3). Outside Great Britain, and in similar circumstances in Great Britain not a prisoner: not a prisoner.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can my State Pension be withheld for a day I am in custody` (Date 1 6 2027) `imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings` FALSE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE FALSE `a sentence of none of those kinds` FALSE FALSE)
-- Outside Great Britain, and in similar circumstances in Great Britain still a prisoner: a prisoner.
#ASSERT `Can my State Pension be withheld for a day I am in custody` (Date 1 6 2027) `imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings` FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE FALSE `a sentence of none of those kinds` FALSE FALSE
-- Line 40: reg 3(1). Remanded in custody and no sentence yet imposed: regulation 2(1) does not apply.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can my State Pension be withheld for a day I am in custody` (Date 1 6 2027) `imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings` TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) TRUE FALSE `a sentence of none of those kinds` FALSE FALSE)
-- Reg 3(2)(a): remanded and later sentenced to imprisonment: regulation 2(1) applies.
#ASSERT `Can my State Pension be withheld for a day I am in custody` (Date 1 6 2027) `imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings` TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) TRUE TRUE `a sentence of imprisonment or detention in legal custody as a result of criminal proceedings` FALSE FALSE
-- Reg 3(2)(c) and fork F6: a suspended sentence is a described sentence, taken as written.
#ASSERT `Can my State Pension be withheld for a day I am in custody` (Date 1 6 2027) `imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings` TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) TRUE TRUE `a suspended sentence within the meaning in section 286 of the Sentencing Code` FALSE FALSE
-- Line 44: reg 3(3). Sentence imposed outside Great Britain that would not have been imposed in similar circumstances in Great Britain: not a described sentence.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can my State Pension be withheld for a day I am in custody` (Date 1 6 2027) `imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings` TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) TRUE TRUE `a sentence of imprisonment or detention in legal custody as a result of criminal proceedings` TRUE TRUE)

§ `Part 3 -- choosing a lump sum or a pension, and deferral`

-- Regulation 4(2): the period is three months starting on the date in the most recent notice (fork F7: 1 March to 31 May).
-- A notice dated 1 March 2026; a choice on 31 May 2026, the last day of the three months.
#ASSERT `Am I within the time to make my choice` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 5 2026) EQUALS `within the period for making the choice`
-- A choice on 1 June 2026, the day after.
#ASSERT `Am I within the time to make my choice` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS `after the period, so that it can only be a late choice`
-- Reg 4(3): no notice yet. The period starts on the later of claiming (1 April) and the death (1 February), and ends on the day of the choice (1 May).
#ASSERT `Am I within the time to make my choice` FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) EQUALS `within the period for making the choice`
-- Fork F10: a choice on 1 March, before the period starts on 1 April. The text says nothing about it.
#ASSERT `Am I within the time to make my choice` FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS `before the period begins, which the text does not provide for`
-- Line 53: reg 4(4). The Secretary of State thinks it reasonable and no lump sum was paid, so there is nothing to repay.
#ASSERT `May I make a late choice` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Reasonable, and a lump sum paid was repaid in full and in the currency paid.
#ASSERT `May I make a late choice` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- A lump sum paid but not repaid in full.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I make a late choice` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- Repaid in full but not in the currency paid.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I make a late choice` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- The Secretary of State does not think it reasonable.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I make a late choice` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Line 56: reg 4(5). A late choice under 4(4) of a state pension reduces the lump sum to nil.
#ASSERT `How much lump sum will I be paid after my choice` 1000 TRUE TRUE EQUALS 0
-- A choice of a state pension that is not a late choice: the lump sum is not reduced by this paragraph.
#ASSERT `How much lump sum will I be paid after my choice` 1000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS 1000
-- A late choice, but of the lump sum: not reduced.
#ASSERT `How much lump sum will I be paid after my choice` 1000 FALSE TRUE EQUALS 1000
-- Line 59: reg 5(2)(a). In writing to an office specified in writing.
#ASSERT `Am I making my choice in a way the Regulations allow` `in writing` TRUE FALSE
-- Reg 5(2)(b). By telephone to a number specified in writing.
#ASSERT `Am I making my choice in a way the Regulations allow` `by telephone` TRUE FALSE
-- Reg 5(3). The Secretary of State directed writing; telephone is not allowed.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I making my choice in a way the Regulations allow` `by telephone` TRUE TRUE)
-- An office the Secretary of State has not specified in writing.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I making my choice in a way the Regulations allow` `in writing` FALSE FALSE)
-- Some other way.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I making my choice in a way the Regulations allow` `in some other way` TRUE FALSE)
-- Lines 65-85: reg 6(2). Applying within three months of the notification, in writing, to change a lump sum to a pension after repaying the lump sum in full, in time and in currency; no earlier change; not treated as made on a death.
#ASSERT `May I change my choice` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 4 2026) FALSE `in writing` TRUE FALSE `a lump sum` `a state pension` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 5000 FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Reg 6(2)(e)(ii). The lump sum was not repaid in the time allowed.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I change my choice` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 4 2026) FALSE `in writing` TRUE FALSE `a lump sum` `a state pension` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 0 5000 FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Reg 6(2)(c). Applying on 1 June, after the three months ended on 31 May, with no longer period allowed.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I change my choice` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) FALSE `in writing` TRUE FALSE `a lump sum` `a state pension` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 5000 FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- The Secretary of State allows a longer period (reg 6(2)(c)(ii)).
#ASSERT `May I change my choice` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE `in writing` TRUE FALSE `a lump sum` `a state pension` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 5000 FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Reg 6(2)(d)(i). The Secretary of State directed writing; the application was by telephone.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I change my choice` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 4 2026) FALSE `by telephone` TRUE TRUE `a lump sum` `a state pension` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 5000 FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Reg 6(2)(f). Changing a pension to a lump sum, where the pension paid so far (3000) is less than the lump sum (5000).
#ASSERT `May I change my choice` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 4 2026) FALSE `in writing` TRUE FALSE `a state pension` `a lump sum` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 3000 5000 FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- The pension paid so far (6000) is not less than the lump sum (5000).
#ASSERT NOT (`May I change my choice` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 4 2026) FALSE `in writing` TRUE FALSE `a state pension` `a lump sum` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 6000 5000 FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Reg 6(2)(g). A previous alteration has been made for the same deferral.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I change my choice` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 4 2026) FALSE `in writing` TRUE FALSE `a lump sum` `a state pension` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 5000 TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- Reg 6(2)(h). The choice was treated as made on a death.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I change my choice` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 4 2026) FALSE `in writing` TRUE FALSE `a lump sum` `a state pension` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 5000 FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Reg 6(2)(b). No application is made.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I change my choice` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 4 2026) FALSE `in writing` TRUE FALSE `a lump sum` `a state pension` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 5000 FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Reg 6(2)(a). The person who made the choice has since died.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I change my choice` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 4 2026) FALSE `in writing` TRUE FALSE `a lump sum` `a state pension` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 5000 FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- Line 87: reg 6(3). The 3000 paid as a pension is treated as paid on account of the 5000 lump sum.
#ASSERT `How much of my lump sum is still to be paid` 5000 3000 EQUALS 2000
-- Nothing paid as a pension so far.
#ASSERT `How much of my lump sum is still to be paid` 5000 0 EQUALS 5000
-- Lines 88-91: reg 7. Entitled, giving notice in writing to a specified office.
#ASSERT `Does my notice suspend my State Pension` TRUE TRUE `in writing` TRUE FALSE
-- By telephone to a specified number.
#ASSERT `Does my notice suspend my State Pension` TRUE TRUE `by telephone` TRUE FALSE
-- Reg 7(3). Writing was directed; telephone is not enough.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my notice suspend my State Pension` TRUE TRUE `by telephone` TRUE TRUE)
-- Reg 7(1). Not yet entitled to a state pension.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my notice suspend my State Pension` FALSE TRUE `in writing` TRUE FALSE)
-- No notice given.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my notice suspend my State Pension` TRUE FALSE `in writing` TRUE FALSE)
-- Lines 92-97: reg 8(3). No date named: the day the option was exercised.
#ASSERT `From what date does my suspension take effect` (Date 1 6 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS (Date 1 6 2027)
-- Reg 8(2). A date named within 28 days starting with the day of the option.
#ASSERT `From what date does my suspension take effect` (Date 1 6 2027) TRUE (Date 10 6 2027) EQUALS (Date 10 6 2027)
-- Fork F8: the last day of the 28 days starting with 1 June is 28 June.
#ASSERT `From what date does my suspension take effect` (Date 1 6 2027) TRUE (Date 28 6 2027) EQUALS (Date 28 6 2027)
-- 29 June is not within the 28 days, so the date is not specified in accordance with 8(2) and 8(3) applies.
#ASSERT `From what date does my suspension take effect` (Date 1 6 2027) TRUE (Date 29 6 2027) EQUALS (Date 1 6 2027)
-- A date before the option was exercised is likewise outside 8(2)(a).
#ASSERT `From what date does my suspension take effect` (Date 1 6 2027) TRUE (Date 31 5 2027) EQUALS (Date 1 6 2027)
-- Lines 98-101: reg 9. Claimed while suspended; a past period within 12 months before 1 June 2027.
#ASSERT `May I cancel my suspension for a past period` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2027) (Date 1 9 2026) (Date 30 11 2026)
-- The period begins more than 12 months before the cancelling date.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I cancel my suspension for a past period` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 6 2027) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 30 11 2026))
-- Reg 9(2). No claim made while the pension was suspended.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I cancel my suspension for a past period` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 6 2027) (Date 1 9 2026) (Date 30 11 2026))
-- Reg 9(1). No option to suspend was exercised.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I cancel my suspension for a past period` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 6 2027) (Date 1 9 2026) (Date 30 11 2026))
-- Line 103: reg 10. One-ninth of 1 per cent.
#ASSERT `What percentage of my weekly pension does each whole week of deferral add` EQUALS (1 / 9) TIMES 1%
-- Regs 10 and 12A(2): one-ninth of 1 per cent of 900 is 1.
#ASSERT `How much does each whole week of my deferral add to my weekly pension` 900 EQUALS 1
-- One-ninth of 1 per cent of 180 is 0.2.
#ASSERT `How much does each whole week of my deferral add to my weekly pension` 180 EQUALS 0.2
-- Regulation 11: a day left out of the weeks of deferral. The sixteen answers are, in order: the benefit received, whether someone received an increase for me, how we are joined, whether either of us is married to a third person, whether we live together, the kind of custody, in Great Britain, similar circumstances, release date certified, the date, remanded, sentenced, kind of sentence, outside Great Britain, similar circumstances, the day.
-- Lines 106-122: reg 11(2)(a). Income support received on the day.
#ASSERT `Is this day left out when my weeks of deferral are counted` `income support` FALSE `not married to each other and not civil partners` FALSE FALSE `in none of those kinds of custody` TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE FALSE `a sentence of none of those kinds` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 6 2027)
-- Reg 11(2)(a)(v).
#ASSERT `Is this day left out when my weeks of deferral are counted` `universal credit` FALSE `not married to each other and not civil partners` FALSE FALSE `in none of those kinds of custody` TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE FALSE `a sentence of none of those kinds` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 6 2027)
-- Reg 11(2)(a)(xi).
#ASSERT `Is this day left out when my weeks of deferral are counted` `incapacity benefit` FALSE `not married to each other and not civil partners` FALSE FALSE `in none of those kinds of custody` TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE FALSE `a sentence of none of those kinds` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 6 2027)
-- No benefit, no increase, no custody.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this day left out when my weeks of deferral are counted` `none of those benefits` FALSE `not married to each other and not civil partners` FALSE FALSE `in none of those kinds of custody` TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE FALSE `a sentence of none of those kinds` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 6 2027))
-- Reg 11(2)(b). Someone received an increase of a listed benefit for me, and is married to me.
#ASSERT `Is this day left out when my weeks of deferral are counted` `none of those benefits` TRUE `married to each other` FALSE FALSE `in none of those kinds of custody` TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE FALSE `a sentence of none of those kinds` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 6 2027)
-- Reg 11(2)(b)(ii). ... or in a civil partnership with me.
#ASSERT `Is this day left out when my weeks of deferral are counted` `none of those benefits` TRUE `civil partners of each other` FALSE FALSE `in none of those kinds of custody` TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE FALSE `a sentence of none of those kinds` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 6 2027)
-- ... or residing with me, though not married or civil partners.
#ASSERT `Is this day left out when my weeks of deferral are counted` `none of those benefits` TRUE `not married to each other and not civil partners` FALSE TRUE `in none of those kinds of custody` TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE FALSE `a sentence of none of those kinds` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 6 2027)
-- None of married, civil partners or residing together.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this day left out when my weeks of deferral are counted` `none of those benefits` TRUE `not married to each other and not civil partners` FALSE FALSE `in none of those kinds of custody` TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE FALSE `a sentence of none of those kinds` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 6 2027))
-- Reg 1(5). One of us is married to a third person, so we are treated as not married to each other, and we do not live together.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this day left out when my weeks of deferral are counted` `none of those benefits` TRUE `married to each other` TRUE FALSE `in none of those kinds of custody` TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE FALSE `a sentence of none of those kinds` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 6 2027))
-- Reg 11(2)(c). A prisoner on the day, who would not have been paid if not deferred.
#ASSERT `Is this day left out when my weeks of deferral are counted` `none of those benefits` FALSE `not married to each other and not civil partners` FALSE FALSE `imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings` TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE FALSE `a sentence of none of those kinds` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 6 2027)
-- Outside Great Britain and not a prisoner in similar circumstances in Great Britain (reg 2(3)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this day left out when my weeks of deferral are counted` `none of those benefits` FALSE `not married to each other and not civil partners` FALSE FALSE `imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings` FALSE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE FALSE `a sentence of none of those kinds` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 6 2027))
-- Lines 123-126: reg 12. 14 days make two whole weeks.
#ASSERT `How many whole weeks of deferral do I have` (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 14 1 2027) 0 EQUALS 2
-- 15 days: the part week at the end is treated as a whole week.
#ASSERT `How many whole weeks of deferral do I have` (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 15 1 2027) 0 EQUALS 3
-- 14 days of which 7 do not count (reg 11): 7 days, one week.
#ASSERT `How many whole weeks of deferral do I have` (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 14 1 2027) 7 EQUALS 1
-- 15 days of which 1 does not count: 14 days, two weeks (fork F12: rounded up once, for the total).
#ASSERT `How many whole weeks of deferral do I have` (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 15 1 2027) 1 EQUALS 2
-- Lines 127-139: reg 12A(3), (4). One non-uprating change on 1 July: the first modification period runs from the start to 30 June; the second from 1 July to the end.
#ASSERT `Into how many stretches is my deferral divided` (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 31 12 2027) TRUE (Date 1 7 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS 2
-- Two changes: three periods.
#ASSERT `Into how many stretches is my deferral divided` (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 31 12 2027) TRUE (Date 1 4 2027) TRUE (Date 1 7 2027) EQUALS 3
-- Reg 12A(1) applies only where the rate changes other than by up-rating, and the periods of (3) and (4) are marked out by those changes; with none there are no modification periods.
#ASSERT `Into how many stretches is my deferral divided` (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 31 12 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS 0

§ `Part 4 -- the minimum number of qualifying years`

-- Lines 141-143: reg 13(1). The minimum is ten.
#ASSERT `Do I have enough qualifying years for a State Pension at the reduced rate` 10
-- Nine is below the minimum.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have enough qualifying years for a State Pension at the reduced rate` 9)
-- Reg 13(2). The minimum is ten.
#ASSERT `Do I have enough qualifying years for a State Pension at the transitional rate` 10
-- Nine is below the minimum.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have enough qualifying years for a State Pension at the transitional rate` 9)

§ `Part 5 -- sharing State Pension rights on divorce or dissolution (the Schedule)`

-- Lines 545-558: inserted reg 6(1)(a), (2), (6). A request for a valuation with no relevant date: a valuation as at the date the request is received, and the explanation.
#ASSERT `What information must the Secretary of State give me when I ask about sharing my State Pension rights` (Date 1 6 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) TRUE EQUALS (LIST `a valuation of the shareable new state scheme rights as at the date the request is received`, `an explanation of the shareable new state scheme rights, of the effect of a pension sharing order or provision, of how the spouse or civil partner becomes entitled, and of how that differs from shared additional pension`)
-- Reg 6(3). A relevant date on or after 6 April 2016: a valuation as at that date, and the explanation.
#ASSERT `What information must the Secretary of State give me when I ask about sharing my State Pension rights` (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE (Date 1 3 2017) TRUE EQUALS (LIST `a valuation of the shareable new state scheme rights as at the relevant date`, `an explanation of the shareable new state scheme rights, of the effect of a pension sharing order or provision, of how the spouse or civil partner becomes entitled, and of how that differs from shared additional pension`)
-- No valuation or amount asked for: the explanation in paragraph (6) only.
#ASSERT `What information must the Secretary of State give me when I ask about sharing my State Pension rights` (Date 1 6 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE EQUALS (LIST `an explanation of the shareable new state scheme rights, of the effect of a pension sharing order or provision, of how the spouse or civil partner becomes entitled, and of how that differs from shared additional pension`)
-- Line 549: inserted reg 6(1)(b). The spouse or civil partner is owed the information in paragraph (6) only.
#ASSERT `What information must the Secretary of State give my spouse or civil partner` EQUALS (LIST `an explanation of the shareable new state scheme rights, of the effect of a pension sharing order or provision, of how the spouse or civil partner becomes entitled, and of how that differs from shared additional pension`)
-- Lines 559-566: inserted reg 6(7)(a). Three months beginning with 1 June 2026 end on 31 August.
#ASSERT `By what date must the Secretary of State give me that information` (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS (Date 31 8 2026)
-- Reg 6(7)(b), fork F13 (the earliest period that applies), fork F7 (counting the first day as day one): six weeks beginning with 1 June end on 12 July.
#ASSERT `By what date must the Secretary of State give me that information` (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS (Date 12 7 2026)
-- Reg 6(7)(c): a shorter period set by the court, here ending 20 June.
#ASSERT `By what date must the Secretary of State give me that information` (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 20 6 2026) EQUALS (Date 20 6 2026)
-- A court period longer than the three months does not shorten it (fork F13).
#ASSERT `By what date must the Secretary of State give me that information` (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 30 9 2026) EQUALS (Date 31 8 2026)
-- Reg 6(8)(a). No valuation or amount asked for: one month beginning with 1 June ends on 30 June.
#ASSERT `By what date must the Secretary of State give me that information` (Date 1 6 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS (Date 30 6 2026)

§ `Part 6 -- a state pension from a late spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit`

-- Reg 15 and 16 shapes used below. Shape (1): the spouse died on 1 March 2015, before 6 April 2016, when I was under pensionable age (mine is 1 June 2025), and I have not married again. Shape (2): the spouse reached pensionable age on 1 January 2015 and died on 1 March 2020, when I was under pensionable age (mine is 1 June 2025). Shape (3): the same, but my pensionable age was 1 January 2019, so I was over it when they died.
-- Lines 148-154: reg 15(1), (2), shape (1). Dead spouse paid graduated contributions; I have reached pensionable age; married when they died, the marriage before 6 April 2016; entitled to an inherited amount under reg 16(1).
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to a state pension based on my late spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit` (Date 1 7 2025) TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 3 2015) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 6 2025) FALSE
-- Reg 15(2)(a). I have not yet reached pensionable age (1 June 2025) on 1 January 2025.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to a state pension based on my late spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit` (Date 1 1 2025) TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 3 2015) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 6 2025) FALSE)
-- Reg 15(1). The dead spouse did not pay graduated contributions as an insured person.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to a state pension based on my late spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit` (Date 1 7 2025) FALSE TRUE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 3 2015) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 6 2025) FALSE)
-- Reg 15(2)(b). We were not married or civil partners when they died.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to a state pension based on my late spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit` (Date 1 7 2025) TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 3 2015) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 6 2025) FALSE)
-- Reg 15(2)(c). The marriage took place after 6 April 2016.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to a state pension based on my late spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit` (Date 1 7 2025) TRUE TRUE (Date 1 5 2016) (Date 1 3 2020) TRUE (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 6 2025) FALSE)
-- Shape (3), reg 16(3): I was over pensionable age when they died, so a later marriage does not matter.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to a state pension based on my late spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit` (Date 1 7 2025) TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 3 2020) TRUE (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2019) TRUE
-- Shape (1) with a later marriage: no inherited amount under 16(1)(c).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to a state pension based on my late spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit` (Date 1 7 2025) TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 3 2015) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 6 2025) TRUE)

§§ `Reg 15(3) and 16: the weekly rate, and the inherited amount`

-- Line 155: reg 15(3), 16(4). Half of a weekly rate of 40 pounds is 20.
#ASSERT `What weekly rate will my state pension under regulation 15 be` (Date 1 7 2025) TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 3 2015) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 6 2025) FALSE 40 EQUALS (JUST 20)
-- No inherited amount, so no pension under reg 15.
#ASSERT `What weekly rate will my state pension under regulation 15 be` (Date 1 7 2025) TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 3 2015) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 6 2025) TRUE 40 EQUALS NOTHING
