§§ `Reg 17: up-rating`

-- The seven answers are: my pension under reg 15, my other state pensions, the full rate before, whether the full rate is increased, what it becomes, whether an uprating order comes into force, and the percentage in it (0.04 is 4 per cent).
-- Lines 187-191: reg 17(3), (4). 20 + 100 is no more than the full rate 200; the full rate rises 5 per cent (200 to 210), so 20 rises by 1.
#ASSERT `By how much will my state pension under regulation 15 rise` 20 100 200 TRUE 210 FALSE 0 EQUALS 1
-- Reg 17(3)(a): equal to the full rate counts. 100 rises 5 per cent.
#ASSERT `By how much will my state pension under regulation 15 rise` 100 100 200 TRUE 210 FALSE 0 EQUALS 5
-- Lines 192-199: reg 17(5), (6). 60 + 160 exceeds 200 and 160 is below it: the shortfall is 40; 5 per cent of 40 is 2.
#ASSERT `By how much will my state pension under regulation 15 rise` 60 160 200 TRUE 210 FALSE 0 EQUALS 2
-- Reg 17(5), (7). The excess is 60 + 160 - 200 = 20; 4 per cent of 20 is 0.8.
#ASSERT `By how much will my state pension under regulation 15 rise` 60 160 200 FALSE 0 TRUE 0.04 EQUALS 0.8
-- Fork F15: both events together are added, 2 + 0.8.
#ASSERT `By how much will my state pension under regulation 15 rise` 60 160 200 TRUE 210 TRUE 0.04 EQUALS 2.8
-- Lines 202-204: reg 17(8), (9). Other pensions 250 are not less than the full rate: the uprating order's 4 per cent of 20 is 0.8.
#ASSERT `By how much will my state pension under regulation 15 rise` 20 250 200 FALSE 0 TRUE 0.04 EQUALS 0.8
-- Nothing happens to the full rate and there is no order: no increase.
#ASSERT `By how much will my state pension under regulation 15 rise` 20 100 200 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS 0

