§ `Part 7 -- living abroad`

-- The eight answers to the first question are: whether Regulations apply reg 21 to this increase, whether my entitlement was deferred, whether I was entitled when it ended, whether I was then an overseas resident, where the increase falls against my deferral, whether I was an overseas resident at the time of the increase, whether I stayed one until the deferral ended, and whether I was entitled just before the increase.
-- Lines 276-280: reg 21(2)(a). No Regulations apply reg 21 to the increase: it does not apply.
#ASSERT `Will an up-rating increase be taken away from me because I live abroad` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `at some other time` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `regulation 21 does not apply to this increase, because no Regulations have been made applying it`
-- Reg 21(5). Entitled and an overseas resident immediately before: the increase is taken away.
#ASSERT `Will an up-rating increase be taken away from me because I live abroad` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `at some other time` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `regulation 21 takes the increase away from the person`
-- Reg 21(5). Entitled, but not an overseas resident.
#ASSERT `Will an up-rating increase be taken away from me because I live abroad` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `at some other time` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `regulation 21 does not take the increase away from the person`
-- Reg 21(5)(a). Not entitled to a state pension immediately before.
#ASSERT `Will an up-rating increase be taken away from me because I live abroad` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `at some other time` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `regulation 21 does not take the increase away from the person`
-- Lines 281-292: reg 21(3), (4)(a). Deferred; entitled and overseas when it ended; an increase in respect of the deferral; I was overseas at the time and stayed so until the end.
#ASSERT `Will an up-rating increase be taken away from me because I live abroad` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `in respect of the deferral period` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `regulation 21 takes the increase away from the person`
-- Reg 21(4)(a)(ii). I did not stay overseas until the deferral ended.
#ASSERT `Will an up-rating increase be taken away from me because I live abroad` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `in respect of the deferral period` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `regulation 21 does not take the increase away from the person`
-- Reg 21(4)(b). An increase after the deferral ended, and I am overseas at the time.
#ASSERT `Will an up-rating increase be taken away from me because I live abroad` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `after the deferral period ended` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `regulation 21 takes the increase away from the person`
-- Reg 21(4)(b). An increase after the deferral ended, but not overseas at the time.
#ASSERT `Will an up-rating increase be taken away from me because I live abroad` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `after the deferral period ended` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `regulation 21 does not take the increase away from the person`
-- Line 293: reg 21(6). A part of the Channel Islands not subject to an Order under section 179.
#ASSERT `Is where I live a territory specified in regulation 21(6)` TRUE FALSE
-- Subject to an Order under section 179.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is where I live a territory specified in regulation 21(6)` TRUE TRUE)
-- Not in the Channel Islands.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is where I live a territory specified in regulation 21(6)` FALSE FALSE)
-- Line 296: reg 22(2). Overseas resident, not in Great Britain nor a specified territory: the rate before the start of the part.
#ASSERT `Which weekly rate is my deferral increment worked from for a part of my deferral` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the weekly rate immediately before the start of the part`
-- Line 297: reg 22(3). Not an overseas resident: the rate before the end of the part.
#ASSERT `Which weekly rate is my deferral increment worked from for a part of my deferral` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the weekly rate immediately before the end of the part`
