#ASSERT `Which weekly rate is my deferral increment worked from for a part of my deferral` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Regulations do not say, because the person was an overseas resident who was in Great Britain or a specified territory`
-- An overseas resident in a Channel Islands part not subject to a section 179 Order: a specified territory, so likewise.
#ASSERT `Which weekly rate is my deferral increment worked from for a part of my deferral` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Regulations do not say, because the person was an overseas resident who was in Great Britain or a specified territory`
-- A Channel Islands part that is subject to a section 179 Order is not a specified territory.
#ASSERT `Which weekly rate is my deferral increment worked from for a part of my deferral` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the weekly rate immediately before the start of the part`
-- Reg 22(2). The rate before the start: 200.
#ASSERT `What weekly rate is my deferral increment worked from for a part of my deferral` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 200 210 EQUALS (JUST 200)
-- Reg 22(3). The rate before the end: 210.
#ASSERT `What weekly rate is my deferral increment worked from for a part of my deferral` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 200 210 EQUALS (JUST 210)
-- Fork F21. The text does not give a rate.
